{
  "title": "Increase SCALAR_LR to 0.8",
  "description": "Increased per-layer scalar learning rate from 0.5 to 0.8 (60% increase) to address undertrained resid_lambdas (0.005 LR) after tuning other parameter groups.",
  "status": "ok",
  "reflection": "Strong improvement of +0.001061 (0.995001 → 0.993940) confirms the pattern: parameter-group LR tuning is the productive direction. Resid_lambdas were undertrained relative to newly-tuned MATRIX_LR (0.05) and UNEMBEDDING_LR (0.008). The 60% increase (0.5→0.8) was aggressive but justified by evidence that larger increases worked well in prior rounds (UNEMBEDDING_LR's 100% increase yielded +0.001220). This validates: (1) the parameter-group rebalancing strategy, (2) that SCALAR_LR was genuinely a bottleneck, and (3) that multiplicative scalars benefit from stronger learning when other components are well-tuned. New best: 0.993940."
}

